  "title": "JK Flip-Flop: The SR Latch With a Useful Fourth Row",
  "eyebrow": "memory and register",
  "language": "en",
  "duration": 53,
  "topic": "JK flip-flop — extends the SR latch by replacing the forbidden S=R=1 state with a TOGGLE mode (Q flips on each rising clock edge when J=K=1). The four modes hold/reset/set/toggle make it the workhorse of binary counters.",
